            <div xml:id="d122">

                <pb facs="0217" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/513–514.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Lorillard to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1908-12-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 468.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence
                    relative to the International Opium Conference, which is to meet at Shanghai on
                    February 1, 1909, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy and a translation
                    of a note from the foreign office, dated the 16th instant, informing me that the
                    Portuguese Government has appointed its consul general at Shanghai, Mr. Oscar
                    George Potier, as its delegate to the conference, and that he will be assisted
                    by the deputy delegate, Mr. Carlos Assumpção.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George Lorillard.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d122-a1.xml" xpointer="d122-a1"/>
            </div>
